present-context-remaining-in-statusline

Lane: frontend

FlatPatch: present-context-remaining-in-statusline

Form: GitDiff

Segment: snapshot

Purpose: Show remaining and total context tokens in the status line without changing terminal-title percentages.

Requires: Unit:frontend/present-account-quota-in-statusline, Unit:frontend/control-model-and-reasoning-with-keyboard

Provides: Render context-remaining from the latest context token usage and positive context window as remaining of total left, omit unknown or pending values, clamp negative usage and exhausted windows, and color only the remaining count using native remaining-percent severity. Match known live preview text and colors while retaining a setup example for unavailable values.

Boundary: Own context-remaining status-line and setup-preview presentation. Preserve token accounting, native context percentages and terminal titles, context-used and legacy identifiers, quota pace, six-cell reasoning and fast labels, selected item order and monochrome rendering. Add no collection or refresh route.

Verification: Focused token-count and unknown-state integration, latest-versus-cumulative usage, exhaustion, runtime windows, title preservation, preview parity, severity boundaries, monochrome and neighboring status-segment tests.


